// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/course/course.t27 -- the t27 course: from zero to a program on a real FPGA
; Source of truth for apps/website/scripts/course-from-spec.mjs (gHashTag/trinity), which
; compiles this file with the vendored compiler (public/t27/t27_compiler.wasm), checks the
; constant schema, evaluates every test block below, checks that every widget a lesson names
; is in specs/widgets/gallery.t27 and that every gallery widget is used by some lesson,
; compiles every lesson spec and refuses one that is not clean, checks the Russian bundle
; named by specs/course/course-ru.t27, and only then writes src/lib/course.generated.ts (the
; page at #/course) and a byte-identical copy of this file at public/learn/course.t27.
; ASCII only (L3), English only (LANG-EN). The Russian words live in the bundle.

; WHAT THE COURSE IS: 27 lessons in 9 modules of 3, for a reader who has never written for a
; chip, then a lab module of 3 lessons on our own research, then a module of 3 on the MX number
; formats AI chips use (OCP Microscaling v1.0). Each lesson is a short text, one working widget from the gallery, and one thing to try
; in it. The widgets are not drawn for the course: they are the same tools a hardware engineer
; uses on t27.ai, built from real runs of t27c, yosys, nextpnr and openFPGALoader on our bench.

; WHAT THE COURSE DOES NOT DO: it says no number of its own. A number a lesson needs is on the
; widget, which names where it came from. The one exception is the t27b figure in lesson 12,
; quoted with its denominator and the run that produced it. The lab lessons quote only the
; rule their widget tests (990 thousandths) and counts that are arithmetic (3 x 3 x 3 = 27).
; The MX lessons quote the constants of the OCP MX v1.0 standard that their widgets compile
; (a block of 32, element widths of 4, 6 and 8 bits, scale code 255 for NaN, bias 127) and
; counts their recording prints.

; WHY 27: the core is 3 cubed lessons, the size of a TRI-27 word. The lab is one more module
; of 3 that reports our own results, and the MX module one more of 3 on the formats the lab
; compares against; both are counted apart so the core stays 27. Changing the
; shape changes the tests.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

